 n\nSoprano Rachel Willis-Sørensen is joined by pianist Tamar Sanikidze fo
 r a recital of late Romantic songs by Rachmaninoff and Strauss\, along wit
 h dramatic 20th-century selections by Korngold\, Kander\, and Previn.\n\nA
  regular presence at the Metropolitan Opera and an audience favorite at Sa
 n Francisco Opera\, Willis-Sørensen has been hailed by the San Francisco 
 Chronicle for her “heroic power and tenderness.” Especially noted as a
  Strauss interpreter\, she was recently honored with the Beverly Sills Art
 ist Award and made her Carnegie Hall recital debut.\n\nThe Shenson Recital
  Series is generously funded by the Drs. Ben and A. Jess Shenson Fund at S
 tanford University.\n\nAdmission Information\n\nTickets: $16.00 – $77.76
